<i><b>Upgrade Notes</b></i>

* Requires NSP V1.39.3 or newer.

<b>V2.27.2 Release</b>

<b>Fixes</b>

* Fix default values for Stage Injection time

* Fix Dash temperature channel sometimes not available.

* Fix ECU temperature not available over Haltech CAN

<b>V2.27.1 Release</b>

<b>Fixes</b>

* Fix <b>Gear Selector Position</b> not displaying correct values on the Dash

* Fix formatted time units not supporting user defined decimal places

* Fix Target Boost Pressure Level showing incorrect value when using Haltech CAN protocol.

* Fix <b>Yaw Rate, Pitch Rate, Roll Rate<b> flicker when enabled in Dash

* Fix <b>Combined Gear Position</b> flickering when <b>Gear Detection Type<b> is configured in Dash

* Fix Knock Sensor 1 Knock Level only allowing percentage units. It now correctly allows decibels.

* Fix dash incorrectly sending DPI state information to Elite ECUs.

* Fix scaling issues in some channels when using <b>Third Party CAN - FuelTech</b>

* Fixes Haltech iC-7 and uC-10 momentary inputs sometimes acting as push-on/push-off when used from an ECU.

<b>V2.27.0 Release</b>

<i><b>Important Notes</b></i>

<b>Features</b>

* Add Wi-Fi support for uC-10

* <b>Fuel Level Sensors</b>
    * Now supports 2 Fuel Level Sensors
    * Add <b>Resistance</b> as an Input Type option for fuel level sensors
    * Increased filtering on fuel level sensors
    * Improved fuel level when sent from ECU to Dash over CAN
        * <b>Fuel Level Remaining</b> channel will represent remaining fuel as a percentage of the total fuel volume as configured in the ECU.
        * <b>Fuel Volume Remaining</b> channel now represents remaining fuel volume as configured in the ECU.
        * The existing <b>Fuel Level</b> channel is now disabled when <i>Sensors - Fuel Level</i> is disabled and all use of the <b>Fuel Level</b> channel on dash screens has been automatically upgraded to use <b>Fuel Level Remaining</b>.

* <b>Third Party Can</b>
    * Support for user configurable baud rates.
    * Support auto detect baud rate.
    * E38 ECU Support
    * Holley EFI Standard Protocol

* Add support for multiple gear detection methods, including:
    * Gear Ratio Detection
    * Gear Position Sensor
    * Selector Position
    * Gear Switch
    * RPM Drop

<b>Fixes</b>

* Fix alarm banners flickering in some instances

* Fix TMS showing <i>Calibrating</i> incorrectly in NSP and dash.

* Fixed occassional loss of logged data when powered off while logging.

* <b>Battery Voltage</b>
    * Change <b>Battery Voltage</b> channel to <b>Device Battery Voltage</b>. This channel always represents the devices measured battery voltage.
    * Add <b>ECU Battery Voltage</b> channel that represents the battery voltage of the ECU connected over CAN.

* Fix the following channels not displaying correctly when sent from a Haltech ECU:
    * Lateral G
    * Longitudinal G
    * Vertical G
    * Pitch Rate
    * Roll Rate
    * Yaw Rate
    * ECU Battery Voltage
    * Fuel Level 1 Volume

* Hide external wideband channels if that wideband is not enabled.

* Fix bar gauges sometimes displaying wrong unit type.

* Fix some channels not displaying correctly when using <b>Syvecs</b> third party protocol.

* Fix a change to a <b>Generic Can</b> channel not notifiying the user that a reset is required.

* Fix Dash Screen Day Palette displayed two times in NSP

* Fix dash sending incorrect DPI state information to Elite ECUs.

* Fixes AVI and SPI input state flickering when state should be on

* Allow <b>Gear Ratio Detection</b> to get <i>RPM</i> and <i>Vehicle Speed</i> from the ECU over CAN but do the gear calculation on the dash if <b>Gear Detection Type</b> is set to anything other than <i>Disabled</i>.

* Fix <b>Transmission - Detection Type - Transmission Ratios</b> showing an error if <b>Driveshaft RPM</b> sensor is disabled in Dash. It now checks if the driveshaft sensor is broadcast by the active CAN protocol.